        "raisedBy": [
          "accessibility"
        ],
        "recommendation": "Keyboard users are trapped (WCAG 2.1.2 No Keyboard Trap, 2.1.1 Keyboard). Once the menu is open, focus moves to its first item; Tab — and Shift+Tab, since the shift key is not checked — is cancelled and wraps around the four items, and no handler closes the menu on Escape. The only way out is to activate an option, which changes the sort order. Per the APG menu button pattern: close the menu on Escape and return focus to the \"Sort\" button; let Tab/Shift+Tab leave the menu (close it without preventDefault) instead of cycling; or use a native <select> with a <label>, which needs none of this code.",
        "reported": true,
        "role": "accessibility",
        "severity": "high",
        "status": "open",
